<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomApplication xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        CustomApplication.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below
        is operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to
        be. Do not paste this back into <description>.

        DPEG Investor Relation is the IR-record-type Lead/Contact/Account population,
        segregated from Acquisitions.

        RECORD PAGE ASSIGNMENT (2026-08-12, amended 2026-08-12 to add the Admin block): the
        dedicated IR Lead record page, Investor_Onboarding_Lead_Record_Page, is assigned here
        via TWO profileActionOverrides blocks below, each scoped to the Lead.Investor_Onboarding
        record type — one for DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access, one for Admin (System Administrator).
        This assignment carries cross-org dependencies that must already exist in the target org
        before this file can deploy there: (a) the DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access profile, (b) the
        System Administrator (Admin) profile, and (c) the Lead.Investor_Onboarding record type.
        Deploying this file to an org missing any of those will fail. These two entries bind the
        page for those TWO profiles only; a user on any other profile will not receive this page
        from either entry and will see the org default record page for that record type instead.
        See the comment directly above the profileActionOverrides blocks for the REPLACE-on-deploy
        hazard this element carries.

        MILESTONE 3 (2026-08-12): the <label> below was changed from the plural "Investor
        Relations" to the singular "Investor Relation" per the user's specified app name.
        THE API NAME (fullName, and therefore this file's name) DELIBERATELY DOES NOT
        CHANGE and stays Investor_Relations. Renaming the API name would deploy as a brand
        new CustomApplication rather than a rename of this one, orphaning every reference
        that already points at Investor_Relations (permission sets, tab settings, this file
        itself) and leaving a duplicate app behind. If a future request asks for the label
        and API name to match, that is a distinct, larger change (new app, migrate
        assignments, retire this one) and not a simple label edit.
    -->
    <brand>
        <headerColor>#0B5394</headerColor>
        <logo>DPEG_Logo_Clear</logo>
        <logoVersion>1</logoVersion>
        <shouldOverrideOrgTheme>true</shouldOverrideOrgTheme>
    </brand>
    <description>DPEG Investor Relation - IR-record-type Lead/Contact/Account population, segregated from Acquisitions. Assigns the Investor Onboarding Lead record page for both the DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access profile and the System Administrator (Admin) profile.</description>
    <formFactors>Large</formFactors>
    <isNavAutoTempTabsDisabled>false</isNavAutoTempTabsDisabled>
    <isNavPersonalizationDisabled>false</isNavPersonalizationDisabled>
    <isNavTabPersistenceDisabled>false</isNavTabPersistenceDisabled>
    <isOmniPinnedViewEnabled>false</isOmniPinnedViewEnabled>
    <label>Investor Relation</label>
    <navType>Standard</navType>
    <!--
        ⚠ profileActionOverrides REPLACES ON DEPLOY, WHOLESALE — it does not merge with the org's
        existing list. Deploying this file overwrites EVERY profileActionOverride the org currently
        has for this app with EXACTLY the blocks listed below and no others. Reconcile this list
        against the live org (e.g. a targeted retrieve of this one CustomApplication) before making
        any future edit here — if a block that exists in the org is missing from this file when it
        is deployed, that assignment is silently deleted with no deploy error.

        BOTH blocks below are required, or an entire profile loses the Investor Onboarding Lead
        record page with no warning:
          - DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access: without it, IR users fall back to the org default Lead
            record page for the Investor_Onboarding record type.
          - Admin (System Administrator): without it, every admin loses the same page — the
            Investor Onboarding Lead record page silently stops rendering for System Administrator
            users, with no deploy error and nothing in the deploy result to indicate why.
    -->
    <profileActionOverrides>
        <actionName>View</actionName>
        <content>Investor_Onboarding_Lead_Record_Page</content>
        <formFactor>Large</formFactor>
        <pageOrSobjectType>Lead</pageOrSobjectType>
        <recordType>Lead.Investor_Onboarding</recordType>
        <type>Flexipage</type>
        <profile>DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access</profile>
    </profileActionOverrides>
    <profileActionOverrides>
        <actionName>View</actionName>
        <content>Investor_Onboarding_Lead_Record_Page</content>
        <formFactor>Large</formFactor>
        <pageOrSobjectType>Lead</pageOrSobjectType>
        <recordType>Lead.Investor_Onboarding</recordType>
        <type>Flexipage</type>
        <profile>Admin</profile>
    </profileActionOverrides>
    <tabs>standard-Lead</tabs>
    <tabs>standard-Contact</tabs>
    <tabs>standard-Account</tabs>
    <tabs>standard-report</tabs>
    <uiType>Lightning</uiType>
</CustomApplication>
